# Publish official draws (non-negotiable)

MatchRead exists so people can see the official tournament and pick it.

## Official seats are always public

The public page shows the **official main-draw sheet**: named players, published byes, and Qualifier/LL TBD seats, in official slot order. That is the draw. Do not wait for TBD seats to be named.

If Tennis API names **both** players in a first-round match, users must **see that match and be able to pick a winner** immediately (`announced_matchups`, `fx-{provider_match_id}`). Partial pairs (named vs Q/LL) stay visible; only the named side is pickable until the TBD is filled.

## Full bracket when the official field exists

When the official first round is published (including 16→32, 32→64, 64→128, or a 96-player Masters as **128 slots + seed byes**), publish a verified draw via `rebuild-draw`. Q/LL TBD and byes count as seats. They do not block publish.

## Still forbidden

- Padding seats the official draw did not publish
- Inventing qualifying winners or bye slots
- Hiding named matches, byes, or TBD seats behind “draw pending” with no list
- Inferring draw size from named-pair count (32 named R128 pairs is not a 64-draw)

Qualifying **matches** are ignored. Qualifier **seats in the main draw** are official and must show. Date-only rows are still seats; times are optional.

## How

- `scripts/publish-draws.mjs` → `rebuild-draw`
- Do not wipe a verified draw to replace it with a weaker one (`force` only for a proven better field)
- `lock_at` still comes from the first timed main-draw ball

This is the other half of pure-fact: fail closed on invented people; fail **open** the moment the official draw exists.
